codex
The current loss already batches classes, but that creates a single replay batch of `shared_classes × num_samples` and retains two full edge-model graphs until the combined SSL backward. On CIFAR-100 that is 3,200 replay examples’ activations per minibatch (current + memory), so the stack can remain in `_engine_run_backward` long enough to look like a deadlock. I’m checking the configured dimensions and tests before changing it to bounded replay chunks with gradient accumulation.
