codex
Autocast is already consistent: both SSL and PRC forwards are inside the same `torch.amp.autocast` block, and one scaler scales their summed loss. Reusing a module in multiple forwards is also supported by autograd, with no `retain_graph` or relevant in-place operation here. The scale-dependent fault is the unbounded PRC replay graph, so I’m bounding its Monte Carlo samples while retaining every shared class and explicitly detaching prototype statistics (PRC should train the representation, not backpropagate into stored prototype history).
